  "summary": "The CDTA and CDTC are wall-mount CO2 detectors with temperature, a setpoint and an override button; the CDTA adds humidity. A DIP switch selects BACnet MS/TP or Modbus RTU. On BACnet the device is an application specific controller (B-ASC) with three analog inputs for the measurements, analog values for setpoints, calculated psychrometrics and calibration offsets, and two binary values.",
